# Workspace Rules & Standards

## 1. Exports & Tree-Shaking
- **NO `export *` STATEMENTS:** Never use wildcard re-exports (`export * from '...'`). It violates tree-shakeable architecture and bloats bundles. Always use explicit, named exports (e.g., `export { Foo, Bar } from './foo';`).

## 2. Errors & Exceptions
- Shared domain errors live in `src/shared/errors/`.
- Domain errors extend `DomainError` with explicit `code`, `message`, and `httpStatus`.
- Validation errors use `ValidationDomainError` with `fieldErrors: Record<string, string[]>`.

## 3. Tool Usage & Persona
- Prefix terminal read operations with `rtk`.
- Terse caveman communication persona.
